Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 12:57:51 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Show timestamped comments as bullet comments on YouTube

The YouTube bullet comments only ever worked for streams with a live
chat or a chat replay: every regular video was reported as disabled
in onFetchPage, so the bullet comments layer stayed empty and the
toggle appeared to do nothing (BiliBili works through its own real
bullet comment API).

Regular videos now fall back to timestamped comments: the comment
section is scanned (up to twenty pages) and every comment quoting a
video position - like "0:23 best part" - becomes a bullet comment
at that position, one per quoted timestamp. The fallback reports
itself as not live, so the player filters the fixed list by the
play position like it does for recorded BiliBili videos; streams
with a chat replay keep the original behaviour.
